Registers grove-g1's SIMULATION-ONLY grasp weld in the vendored unitree_mujoco.

Generated against unitree_mujoco ae6a8403e272733e9996ef59990880330496177f, on top of
001 and 004 (whose main.cc context this diff includes).

The weld manager's own source is COPYed in by the Dockerfile and is NOT part of this patch,
so this stays a registration hook: an include, a start, two stops, and one source file added
to the target. simulate/src/unitree_sdk2_bridge.h is untouched.

Started from main() rather than from the bridge thread, unlike 004: this needs sim->mtx and
opens no DDS channels, so it belongs beside the sensor sampler that has the same requirement.

Stopped at both model-replacement paths (the viewer's Reload button and drag-and-drop) with
a blocking join, before mj_deleteModel, because it caches equality and body ids resolved
against the old model. It is not restarted afterwards, so a reload ends with nothing held.

What it exists for: patch 003 gives the fingers no contact geometry on purpose, so a closed
hand passes through an object and the scene never sees a grasp. This welds the object to the
palm once the fingers have measurably closed near it. On hardware that job belongs to
friction, and this file never runs -- its thresholds are properties of the weld, not of the
Dex3's grip, and are on the hardware re-validation list rather than being carried over.

